menu "Micro OS network"

    config MICRO_OS_NET
        bool "the network services of the board"
        default y
        help
            The HTTP client, the clock from NTP, the page of the state and
            the MQTT client. The sockets come from the port; the protocols
            are portable and are tested on the host. Turn this off for an
            image that has no network at all: no source of the component is
            compiled and no command of it is registered.

    config MICRO_OS_NET_HTTP
        bool "the HTTP client and the http command"
        depends on MICRO_OS_NET
        default y
        help
            GET a URL and print the status and the body: the command
            "http get <url>", and the transport the page of the state uses.

    config MICRO_OS_NET_HTTP_SERVER
        bool "the page of the state (httpd)"
        depends on MICRO_OS_NET
        default n
        help
            The page on port 80 that a person starts with "httpd". It is off
            by default: a command a person starts is a feature of the
            session, not of the boot, and the listener task costs the static
            memory of the board.

    config MICRO_OS_NET_NTP
        bool "the clock from NTP and the ntp command"
        depends on MICRO_OS_NET
        default y
        help
            Ask an NTP server for the time of Unix and give it to the clock
            of the board. A board without a network to a time server can
            leave it out.

    config MICRO_OS_NET_MQTT
        bool "the MQTT client and the mqtt command"
        depends on MICRO_OS_NET
        default n
        help
            Publish one message over MQTT 3.1.1. Off by default: the board
            has no broker of its own, and a release that wants the client
            turns it on in sdkconfig.defaults (ADR 0010).

endmenu
